{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `r`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `r` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, `r ~ binomial_logit(n, b);`. The other data variables, `N` and `n`, are context inputs used as a size and binomial-trials predictor. All parameters have exactly one built-in prior before use in the model block.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int r;
  array[N] int n;
}
parameters {
  real mu;
  real<lower=0> sigmasq;
  array[N] real b;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  array[N] real<lower=0, upper=1> p;
  sigma = sqrt(sigmasq);
  for (i in 1 : N) {
    p[i] = inv_logit(b[i]);
  }
}
model {
  mu ~ normal(0.0, 1000.0);
  sigmasq ~ inv_gamma(0.001, 0.001);
  b ~ normal(mu, sigma);
  r ~ binomial_logit(n, b);
}
generated quantities {
  real pop_mean;
  pop_mean = inv_logit(mu);
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "N": 1,
  "n": [
    2
  ],
  "r": [
    2
  ]
}
","protected_variables":["r"]}
